# better-sqlite3 ships N-API prebuilt binaries for every platform in its tarball
# (node_modules/better-sqlite3/prebuilds/*.node). Package managers still run an
# implicit `node-gyp rebuild` for any package containing a binding.gyp, which on a
# machine without MSVC fails the whole install -- and on a machine with a compiler
# silently wastes minutes building a binary that is already there.
#
# Turning install scripts off makes the prebuild the only path. Verified by a
# clean install on Windows + Node 24 with no toolchain, and asserted in
# tests/conventions/package-manager.test.ts.
#
# The tradeoff, stated: no dependency postinstall runs. Nothing in this tree needs
# one (esbuild ships its binary via optionalDependencies). If a future dependency
# genuinely requires a postinstall, approve it explicitly rather than removing this.
ignore-scripts=true
